B.Db=new A.n(1,0.8980392156862745,0.45098039215686275,0.45098039215686275,B.e)
B.De=new A.n(0.3764705882352941,0.09803921568627451,0.09803921568627451,0.09803921568627451,B.e)
B.Dh=new A.n(1,0.1607843137254902,0.47058823529411764,0.7098039215686275,B.e)
B.Dm=new A.n(0.9411764705882353,0.7529411764705882,0.7529411764705882,0.7529411764705882,B.e)
B.mJ=new A.n(1,0.12156862745098039,0.1607843137254902,0.21568627450980393,B.e)
B.Dr=new A.bu("Combination","Nitric acid (HNO\u2083) is a strong acid used to make fertilizers and explosives.","Two HNO\u2083 need 2 H, 2 N and 6 O. That is one H\u2082, one N\u2082 and three O\u2082 (3 \xd7 2 = 6 oxygens).")
B.Ds=new A.bu("Combination","Carbon dioxide (CO\u2082) is the gas you breathe out. Plants take it in to make food, and it puts the bubbles in soda.","Already balanced: 1 carbon and 2 oxygen atoms on each side.")
B.Dt=new A.bu("Combination","Sodium sulfide (Na\u2082S) is used in paper making and leather work. It smells like rotten eggs when it gets wet.","Each Na\u2082S has 2 Na and 1 S, so every sulfur atom takes 2 sodium atoms.")
B.Du=new A.bu("Combination","Water (H\u2082O) is essential for life. Burning hydrogen gas makes nothing but water, which is why hydrogen is a clean fuel.","O\u2082 brings 2 oxygens, so we make 2 H\u2082O. Those hold 4 hydrogens, which is 2 H\u2082.")
B.Dv=new A.bu("Combination","Hydrogen chloride (HCl) is a gas that becomes hydrochloric acid in water. Your stomach makes a weak version to break down food.","H\u2082 and Cl\u2082 each have 2 atoms, but one HCl has 1 of each. Making 2 HCl uses every atom.")
B.Dw=new A.bu("Combination","Hydrogen sulfide (H\u2082S) is the gas that smells like rotten eggs. It bubbles out of swamps and volcanoes.","Already balanced: 2 hydrogens and 1 sulfur on each side.")
B.Dx=new A.bu("Combination","Iron oxide (Fe\u2082O\u2083) is rust, the orange-brown flaky coating on iron left in damp air. It is why bikes and nails rust.","Each Fe\u2082O\u2083 has 2 Fe and 3 O. 3 O\u2082 gives 6 oxygens, which makes 2 Fe\u2082O\u2083 and takes 4 Fe.")
B.Dy=new A.bu("Combination","Sodium carbonate (Na\u2082CO\u2083), or washing soda, softens water in laundry and is used to make glass.","Each Na\u2082CO\u2083 has 2 Na, 1 C and 3 O. To use whole O\u2082 pairs, make 2 Na\u2082CO\u2083: that is 4 Na, 2 C and 6 O (3 O\u2082).")
B.Dz=new A.bu("Metal + Water","Sodium hydroxide (NaOH), also called lye, is a strong base used to make soap and clear drains. Sodium fizzes wildly in water, makes hydrogen gas and gets very hot.","Two NaOH hold 2 Na, 2 O and 2 H. The O comes from 2 H\u2082O; of the 4 H in that water, 2 go into NaOH and 2 escape as H\u2082 gas.")
B.DA=new A.bu("Combination","Sodium bicarbonate (NaHCO\u2083) is baking soda. It makes cakes rise by releasing CO\u2082 bubbles, and it cleans and removes odors.","Each NaHCO\u2083 has 1 Na, 1 H, 1 C and 3 O. Making 2 NaHCO\u2083 uses 2 Na, 2 C, 6 O (3 O\u2082) and 2 H (1 H\u2082).")
B.DB=new A.bu("Combination","Phosphorus pentoxide (P\u2082O\u2085) is a white powder that soaks up water so strongly it is used to dry out other chemicals.","Two P\u2082O\u2085 hold 4 P and 10 O. That is 4 P atoms and 5 O\u2082 pairs (5 \xd7 2 = 10 oxygens).")
B.DC=new A.bu("Combination","Sodium oxide (Na\u2082O) is a white solid that makes sodium hydroxide when it meets water. It is used in glass making.","Each Na\u2082O has 2 Na and 1 O. O\u2082 brings 2 oxygens, so we make 2 Na\u2082O, which takes 4 Na.")
B.DD=new A.bu("Combination","Calcium carbonate (CaCO\u2083) is found in chalk, limestone and seashells. It is also the main ingredient in some antacid tablets.","Each CaCO\u2083 has 1 Ca, 1 C and 3 O. To use whole O\u2082 pairs, make 2 CaCO\u2083: that is 2 Ca, 2 C and 6 O (3 O\u2082).")
B.DE=new A.bu("Combination","Potassium carbonate (K\u2082CO\u2083), or potash, was once made from wood ashes. It is used in soap and glass.","Each K\u2082CO\u2083 has 2 K, 1 C and 3 O. To use whole O\u2082 pairs, make 2 K\u2082CO\u2083: that is 4 K, 2 C and 6 O (3 O\u2082).")
B.DF=new A.bu("Combination","Ammonia (NH\u2083) is a sharp-smelling gas used to make fertilizer that helps grow food. Factories pull the nitrogen from the air.","N\u2082 has 2 nitrogens, so we make 2 NH\u2083. Those hold 6 hydrogens, which is 3 H\u2082.")
B.DG=new A.bu("Combination","Hydrogen bromide (HBr) is a gas that forms hydrobromic acid in water, a strong acid used to make other chemicals.","H\u2082 and Br\u2082 each have 2 atoms, but one HBr has 1 of each. Making 2 HBr uses every atom.")
B.DH=new A.bu("Combination","Magnesium carbonate (MgCO\u2083) is the white chalk that gymnasts and climbers rub on their hands for grip.","Each MgCO\u2083 has 1 Mg, 1 C and 3 O. To use whole O\u2082 pairs, make 2 MgCO\u2083: that is 2 Mg, 2 C and 6 O (3 O\u2082).")
B.DI=new A.bu("Combination","Methane (CH\u2084) is the main gas in natural gas, used for cooking and heating. Swamps and cows make it too.","Hydrogen travels in H\u2082 pairs. One carbon needs 4 hydrogens to make CH\u2084, which is 2 H\u2082.")
B.DJ=new A.bu("Combination","Silver oxide (Ag\u2082O) is a dark powder used in small silver-oxide batteries inside watches.","Each Ag\u2082O has 2 Ag and 1 O. O\u2082 brings 2 oxygens, so we make 2 Ag\u2082O, which takes 4 Ag.")
B.DK=new A.bu("Combination","Sulfur dioxide (SO\u2082) is a sharp-smelling gas from volcanoes and burning coal. It causes acid rain, and tiny amounts keep dried fruit from spoiling.","Already balanced: 1 sulfur and 2 oxygen atoms on each side.")
B.DL=new A.bu("Combination","Boron oxide (B\u2082O\u2083) is a glassy solid used to make heat-resistant glass for ovens and lab equipment.","Each B\u2082O\u2083 has 2 B and 3 O. 3 O\u2082 gives 6 oxygens, which makes 2 B\u2082O\u2083 and takes 4 B.")
B.DM=new A.bu("Combination","Phosphoric acid (H\u2083PO\u2084) gives cola its tangy taste. It is also used in fertilizer and rust remover.","Phosphorus comes as P\u2084, so we make 4 H\u2083PO\u2084. That needs 12 H and 16 O: 10 O come from 5 O\u2082 and the other 6 O (plus all 12 H) come from 6 H\u2082O.")
B.DN=new A.bu("Acid Reaction","Limestone fizzes when acid touches it, giving off carbon dioxide. This is why acid rain slowly wears away marble statues.","CaCO\u2083 has 1 Ca, 1 C and 3 O. The 2 Cl from 2 HCl go into CaCl\u2082, and the 2 H join one O to form H\u2082O. The other 2 O make CO\u2082.")
B.DO=new A.bu("Combination","Calcium carbide (CaC\u2082) is a gray solid. Add water and it releases acetylene gas, which fueled old miners' lamps.","CaC\u2082 holds 1 Ca and 2 C, so we need 2 carbon atoms for every calcium.")
B.DP=new A.bu("Combination","Potassium oxide (K\u2082O) is a reactive solid that turns into potassium hydroxide in water. It is how potash fertilizer is measured.","Each K\u2082O has 2 K and 1 O. O\u2082 brings 2 oxygens, so we make 2 K\u2082O, which takes 4 K.")
B.DQ=new A.bu("Combination","Sulfuric acid (H\u2082SO\u2084) is one of the most-made chemicals in the world. It is used in car batteries and fertilizer, and it is very strong, so it is only used by trained people.","One H\u2082SO\u2084 needs 2 H, 1 S and 4 O. That is one H\u2082, one S and two O\u2082 (2 \xd7 2 = 4 oxygens).")
B.DR=new A.bu("Combination","Hydrogen fluoride (HF) dissolves in water to make hydrofluoric acid, a strong acid that can etch glass. It is handled very carefully.","H\u2082 and F\u2082 each have 2 atoms, but one HF has 1 of each. Making 2 HF uses every atom.")
B.DS=new A.bu("Combustion","Burning methane is what a gas stove does. The flame releases heat and the only leftovers are carbon dioxide and water vapor.","Carbon goes to CO\u2082 (1 C). Hydrogen goes to water, so 4 H makes 2 H\u2082O. The products hold 4 O, so we need 2 O\u2082.")
B.DT=new A.bu("Combination","Hydrogen iodide (HI) forms hydroiodic acid in water, a strong acid used in laboratories.","H\u2082 and I\u2082 each have 2 atoms, but one HI has 1 of each. Making 2 HI uses every atom.")
B.DU=new A.bu("Combination","Lithium oxide (Li\u2082O) is a white solid used in special glass and ceramics. Lithium is also the metal inside rechargeable batteries.","Each Li\u2082O has 2 Li and 1 O. O\u2082 brings 2 oxygens, so we make 2 Li\u2082O, which takes 4 Li.")
B.DV=new A.bu("Acid Reaction","Baking soda fizzes when it meets an acid. Here the acid is hydrochloric acid, and the bubbles are carbon dioxide gas. It is the same fizz as a baking soda volcano.","Already balanced: 1 Na, 1 Cl, 1 C, 2 H and 3 O on each side. The atoms just trade partners.")
B.DW=new A.bu("Combination","Barium carbonate (BaCO\u2083) is a white powder used in ceramics and glass. It is poisonous.","Each BaCO\u2083 has 1 Ba, 1 C and 3 O. To use whole O\u2082 pairs, make 2 BaCO\u2083: that is 2 Ba, 2 C and 6 O (3 O\u2082).")
B.DX=new A.bu("Combination","Magnesium nitride (Mg\u2083N\u2082) forms when magnesium burns in air, because air is mostly nitrogen. With water it gives off ammonia.","Mg\u2083N\u2082 holds 3 Mg and 2 N, and N\u2082 is already a pair of nitrogens. So 3 Mg meets 1 N\u2082.")
B.DY=new A.bu("Combination","Aluminum oxide (Al\u2082O\u2083) forms a thin hard layer on aluminum that protects it. Rubies, sapphires and sandpaper are made of it.","Each Al\u2082O\u2083 has 2 Al and 3 O. 3 O\u2082 gives 6 oxygens, which makes 2 Al\u2082O\u2083 and takes 4 Al.")
