B.Gg=new A.eF("Mix and watch","Crystal Growing","Grow sparkly sugar crystals on a stick.",B.YJ,B.FT,B.JG,!1,B.na,"Crystal color",5,"Crystallization",null,"Warm water can dissolve a lot of sugar. As the water cools and slowly dries up, the sugar has nowhere to go. The sugar pieces line up in neat patterns on the stick, and those patterns are crystals.","Nothing new is made. It is the same sugar, just rearranged. That is called a physical change, so there is no equation.","Five days later: crystals grew all over the stick!",5000,!1)
